Package: mascot
Title: Live Mood-Driven Mascots for 'Shiny' Apps and 'Quarto' Sites
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Harsh", "Verma", email = "analyticswithharsh@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Adds a character drawn in code to 'Shiny' apps and 'Quarto'
    sites. The character shows a mood with a status text beside it and
    animates when the mood changes; a 'Shiny' server can change its mood,
    status, speech bubble and gestures, and a click can run an action or
    open a menu. It follows light and dark mode and takes its colours from
    built-in palettes, your own colours or a 'bslib' theme. You can describe
    your own characters in 'JSON' and check them before use, and a local
    studio app demonstrates every function. It works offline: the drawing is
    done in the browser from bundled 'JavaScript'.
